WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.834
This comparison is worth learning conceptually
GROUPING SETS produces

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:11.433
only the grouping combinations you request ROLLUP of
A and B produces

00:00:11.459 --> 00:00:14.656
detail at A and B a subtotal at A and a grand

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:20.681
total It follows a hierarchy CUBE of A and B
produces

00:00:20.707 --> 00:00:25.947
detail subtotals by A subtotals by B and the grand
total It

00:00:25.973 --> 00:00:31.453
generates every combination A simple way to choose
is to ask what

00:00:31.479 --> 00:00:36.869
report levels you need If you need a hierarchy
ROLLUP is often

00:00:36.895 --> 00:00:43.029
a natural fit If you need all cross-dimensional
totals consider CUBE If

00:00:43.056 --> 00:00:49.062
you want only specific levels GROUPING SETS gives
you precise control The

00:00:49.089 --> 00:00:53.036
SQL syntax is different but the same grain reasoning
still applies to

00:00:53.049 --> 00:00:54.141
every row produced
